    relieve_ley: (a, b) => `Elevation in view: ${a} to ${b} m`,
    sim_metodo: "2D hydraulic model (local inertial approximation of the shallow water equations, the same family as LISFLOOD-FP and the HEC-RAS 2D diffusion wave), hour by hour. It starts 14 days back with real rain, so soil and ponds reach today as they are; then hourly forecast (16 days) and, beyond, the monthly seasonal forecast spread over the place's typical rain days. In each cell: rain, infiltration (Green-Ampt, by soil and moisture), drains, evaporation and runoff downhill with roughness by land cover. Ponds store water; rivers have a fixed (adjustable) level. Tested against theory (sloped plane) with exact water balance. It does not include the real drainage network (no data outside Buenos Aires City) and satellite terrain has 1-3 m errors: it is indicative, not an official flood forecast.", idioma_aria: "Cambiar el idioma a español", tema_aria: "Switch between light and dark theme",
