    sim_peor_calc: (k, n) => `Working out which El Niño affected the most people here… ${k} of ${n}`, sim_peor_estimando: "Estimating which El Niño was worst for people…", sim_peor_sin_datos: "The worst El Niño could not be estimated: there is no rain data for this place.", sim_peor_res: (tp, p, ha) => `▲ Estimated worst for people: ${tp} · ~${p} people with 10 cm of water or more (${ha} ha)`, sim_peor_res0: (tp) => `▲ No El Niño leaves 10 cm of water where people live; the one that pools the most water is ${tp}`, sim_peor_ayuda: "Estimated with a formula, without simulating the water. For each El Niño's worst storm (IMERG satellite, hour by hour): soil runoff with the Curve Number method (initial abstraction 0.05 S, Hawkins et al. 2002) from its texture and how wet it was just before; on paved ground, each hour's rain above storm-drain capacity; that water fills the terrain's low spots until they spill; and the river on those same days enters the land connected to it that lies below its level. It counts census-tract residents with 10 cm of water or more and flags the El Niño with the most.", sim_mm_en_3d: (mm) => `${mm} mm in 3 days`, sim_bajando_tormenta: "Downloading the storm hour by hour…",
